{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/171092-help-locating-information-i-saw-a-while-back-werewolf-enforcer","id":171092,"title":"Help locating information I saw a while back (Werewolf \"enforcer\")","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-16T15:24:19-07:00","id":171092,"title":"Help locating information I saw a while back (Werewolf \"enforcer\")","content":"Hi first time caller, long time listener...<br /> First off I'm still relatively new to anything WoD outside of the core rule book, though I do own the core rulebooks for WtF, MtA, and VtR. But still I am quite unfamiliar with many aspects, though I am trying very hard to learn as I go.<br /> <br /> On to the Short story/explanation: Quite a while ago (about a year and a half ago) I was planning a WoD campaign (that ultimately fell through). Now I have another chance at running a campaign and I have been wracking my brain trying to find that specific werewolf ruling. <br /> Anyways I was helping a friend stat a character that would occasionally be a guest NPC. The friend wanted the character to be an enforcer of sorts. Someone who did the dirty job of punishing werewolves who stepped out of line/severely broke the rules. So I went searching. First I read up on the Elodoth and how they are often considered Judges which was on the right track but not quite what they wanted so I dug deeper. And a little while later I found in one of the books at the local game shop almost exactly what my friend was looking for. It was a judge/enforcer of sorts but the thing that stood out to me was they were expected to carry silver weapons as part of their duty, and I want to say they were overlooked or forgiven for this act because of the job they did.<br /> <br /> But now the game shop I used to frequent has cleared out their entire WoD book section. (now replaced with Pathfinder ugggh) And my campaign planning notes were all destroyed when the basement flooded during the last hurricane that hit my area. (Also all my internet search attempts have so far been in vain) Now I have no clue where to turn next and it occurred to me, why not turn to people far more savvy with the rules then myself. I would like to narrow down the book so I can order it online, because I like having a physical copy, Though if my hand is forced I will download it from that drivethru site.<br /> Granted It is possible that I read it in one of the Apocalypse books by accident because at the time I did not realize the the difference between the printings of Apocalypse and Forsaken. But I feel like it was in one of the nWtF books.I don't know anymore. So can any of you please help me?<br /> <br /> Thank you very much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3313-phoenix-wombat","name":"Phoenix Wombat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T15:42:19-07:00","id":171138,"title":"","content":"Sounds like it might be the Secret Tribunal, from Signs of the Moon. I'm not sure if they get special dispensation to use silver, but in the examples of their 'work' it suggests they've cut the hands off Uratha with silver knives for selling out their pack to vampires. They act as a sort of secret police, judging and punishing crimes that otherwise would go unjudged or unpunished.<br /> <br /> They're an elodoth lodge. They don't get any special bonus to resist harmony loss when using silver in combat, though, and they're a secret lodge so most people wouldn't know to look away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8